The diff is clean and correct. Here's a summary of the bug and the fix:

## Bug Analysis

**Root Cause:** In `DocumentEditFragment.onResume()`, when the user switches back to the app, the method called `_hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent())` to sync the editor with the document content. However, `setText()` on an `EditText` (which `HighlightingEditor` extends) **resets the cursor/selection to position 0**. The cursor position was never saved and restored after the `setText()` call.

**Why it happens:** Android's `TextView.setText()` method clears the selection state. Without explicitly saving and restoring the cursor position, it always jumps back to the beginning of the text.

## The Fix

The fix preserves the cursor position using the same pattern already used in `loadDocumentIntoUi()` (lines 135-138 of the same file):

1. **Before `setText()`**: Save the current cursor position via `getSelectionStart()`
2. **Call `setText()`**: Update the content (this resets cursor to 0)
3. **After `setText()`**: Clamp the saved position to the new text length and restore it via `setSelection()`

## Patch

```diff
--- a/app/src/main/java/net/gsantner/markor/activity/DocumentEditFragment.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/net/gsantner/markor/activity/DocumentEditFragment.java
@@ -109,7 +109,10 @@ public class DocumentEditFragment extends BaseFragment implements TextFormat.Text
     public void onResume() {
         super.onResume();
         checkReloadDisk();
+        int editorpos = _hlEditor.getSelectionStart();
         _hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());
+        editorpos = editorpos > _hlEditor.length() ? _hlEditor.length() - 1 : editorpos;
+        _hlEditor.setSelection(editorpos < 0 ? 0 : editorpos);
     }
```

The build failed due to network restrictions in this environment (can't reach jcenter.bintray.com), which is an infrastructure limitation unrelated to the code change. The code change itself is syntactically correct and follows the exact same cursor-preservation pattern already proven to work in `loadDocumentIntoUi()` within the same file.

